	quest.3029E1E133B91ED8.quest_desc: ["The &n&5Drill&r will break any block in front of it. If it has a connected inventory, the items will be stored in it."]
	quest.32117ADBFD9B230A.quest_desc: ["Flint Meshes—now these are the real deal. When used with gravel, they can yield your first real materials like iron, diamonds, emeralds, and more. However, the drop rates aren’t great, so once you get some iron, it’s a smart move to upgrade your meshes for better efficiency."]
	quest.3247179F0F0252A2.quest_desc: ["{atm9.quest.storage.desc.ender}"]
	quest.3247179F0F0252A2.title: "{atm9.quest.storage.ender}"
	quest.3314FBC4FEAE1D08.quest_desc: ["The &n&5Deployer&r can be used to either place items/blocks or to use items like Swords."]
	quest.33882172DA8021F6.quest_subtitle: "{atm9.quest.storage.subt.refill}"
	quest.33882172DA8021F6.title: "{atm9.quest.storage.refill}"
	quest.342B3DD82822DC35.quest_desc: ["The trader block allows trading with the villager without having to deal with securing the villager. This block also allows the villager to restock in non-working hours. The restocking time of the villager is not dependent on any external sources like day/night time or dimension."]
	quest.35C6DD81DA6D9754.quest_desc: [
		"This mod can definitely be a bit confusing at first, but once you get the hang of it, it’s not too hard to follow."
		""
		"To get started, you’ll need to wait for the wandering villager from the mod to spawn — that’s how you choose your storyline. You can pick between Radical Red and Shining Pearl, but I recommend going with Radical Red for the most competitive and challenging experience."
		""
		"You’ll earn badges as you progress, and these are essential for advancing through the mod. There’s also a level cap system, so make sure not to catch or level up any Pokémon above the current cap — it starts at Level 15 for the first gym leader."
		""
		"In the Radical Red path, your first gym leader is Brock, so be prepared! This mod doesn't go easy on you — expect a real challenge."
		""
		"If you ever get stuck or need more info, check the in-game Trainer Card or head over to the mod’s wiki — both are great sources of up-to-date guidance."
	]
	quest.35C6DD81DA6D9754.title: "StoryMode"
	quest.35E8C65CCA676E76.title: "{atm9.quest.SG.chestplate}"
	quest.3616507498A925D8.quest_desc: [
		"In time, you’ll come across a chest containing a few saplings. Don’t worry—you can always collect more as you go. This is just the beginning of your journey, so take your time and enjoy the process."
		"Place it next to the chests to connect with the crafting table—think of it as a small starter storage system to help you stay organized"
	]
	quest.361DFDB1E1352D6B.quest_desc: ["{atm9.quest.farm.desc.cane}"]
	quest.361DFDB1E1352D6B.quest_subtitle: "{atm9.quest.farm.subt.cane}"
	quest.361DFDB1E1352D6B.title: "{atm9.quest.farm.cane}"
	quest.36BCE35215B2B6E9.title: "{atm9.quest.storage.Asmoking}"
	quest.3722B43822F80470.quest_desc: ["{atm9.quest.SG.desc.katana}"]
	quest.3722B43822F80470.quest_subtitle: "{atm9.quest.SG.subt.katana}"
	quest.3722B43822F80470.title: "{atm9.quest.SG.katana}"
	quest.3783BECAA085F10B.quest_desc: [
		"One Block Phases Overview"
		"The One Block experience is broken into multiple phases, each with its own unique theme and resources. Here's the full list:"
		""
		"Phase 0: Tutorial"
		""
		"Phase 1: The Plains"
		""
		"Phase 2: The Underground"
		""
		"Phase 3: Icy Tundra"
		""
		"Phase 4: Steaminess (New)"
		""
		"Phase 5: Ocean"
		""
		"Phase 6: Jungle Dungeon"
		""
		"Phase 7: Red Desert"
		""
		"Phase 8: The Nether"
		""
		"Phase 9: Idyll"
		""
		"Phase 10: Travel (New)"
		""
		"Phase 11: Desolate Land"
		""
		"Phase 12: Subterranean Depths (New)"
		""
		"Phase 13: The End"
		""
		"Don’t worry — after Phase 13, there is an \"after phase\", meaning the experience becomes endless, so you can keep playing beyond the final listed stage."
		""
		"Important Notes:"
		"Phases Do Not Repeat: Once you move past a phase, you can’t go back to it. Be sure to gather any resources you need before advancing to the next phase."
		""
		"Don’t Rely Solely on the One Block: While it’s your main source of materials, you’ll need to explore and use other methods to obtain what you need."
		""
		"Cobblmon Spawning:"
		"Cobblmon spawn naturally on their appropriate blocks and in their natural biomes. For the best spawn rates:"
		""
		"Build a large grass platform (especially early on)."
		""
		"Don’t expect every Cobblmon to spawn from the one block itself — biomes still matter."
		""
		"Finding Biomes:"
		"You’ll still need to explore to locate different biomes. To make this easier:"
		""
		"Use the Nature’s Compass mod to find specific biomes more efficiently."
		""
		"Consider building natural environments (e.g. swamps, jungles, oceans) around your base to encourage the Cobblmon you’re looking for to spawn."
	]
	quest.3783BECAA085F10B.title: "OneBlock"
